{"seconds": 31.3, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! White wins the queen (9 points). Black's forced reply is Kxd8 or Rxd8, but either way White is up a full queen. This is a crushing win.\n\n**Summary:**\n\n**Best move:** Nxe6\n\n**Main line:** \n1. Nxe6 Bxe6 \n2. Rxd8+ Kxd8 (or Rxd8)\n3. White wins the queen\n\n**Motif:** pin\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nWhen a rook pins a bishop to the queen on the same file, look for a forcing sequence using the pin. Here, Nxe6 exploits the pin brilliantly\u2014the pinned bishop on d7 cannot capture back, so after Bxe6 (the only way to avoid disaster), Rxd8+ wins the queen outright. The lesson: **work the pin by attacking the pinned piece again with extra pieces, and it often leads to tactical wins.**\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nxe6\", \"line\": [\"Nxe6\", \"Bxe6\", \"Rxd8+\", \"Kxd8\"], \"motifs\": [\"pin\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "square": "d1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "square": "h1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "square": "f4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "square": "f3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "square": "d8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "square": "a8"}}, {"tool": "chess-